## External integration status

Supabase request construction and upsert behavior were verified with a mocked HTTP response. A live write was
not attempted because SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_KEY were not present in the process environment. Apply
supabase/migrations/001_create_episodes.sql and inject both variables into a trusted shell/CI environment before
running `python scripts/run_pilot.py tests/fixtures/episode_sample.json --backend supabase`.

## 2026-08-31 Logging/OAuth regression

PASS (10 unit/adapter tests)

- Rotating `pipeline.log` creation and UTF-8 event persistence verified.
- FFmpeg stdout/stderr isolation into `ffmpeg.log` verified with a subprocess fixture.
- Missing FFmpeg executable produces both a traceback in `pipeline.log` and an actionable `ffmpeg.log`.
- Revoked refresh token fixture produces `YouTubeAuthenticationError` with re-authorization guidance.
- Missing video is no longer reported as a mock upload success.
- Live YouTube upload was not attempted; replacing the revoked Actions secret requires channel-owner OAuth.

## 2026-08-31 Story-to-video pilot

PASS (contract and adapter level; 13 unit/adapter tests)

- The supplied three-sequence story transitions from `SCRIPT_READY` to `RENDERED`.
- Output contract checks H.264/AAC streams, 1080x1920 resolution and 30 seconds ±0.5 seconds.
- Local manifest records video SHA-256, duration, dimensions and codecs.
- Supabase PATCH is guarded by both `episode_id` and the source `content_hash`.
- Landscape output is rejected before the `RENDERED` state update.

The current development container has no FFmpeg binary. Installation was attempted, but its Ubuntu package
repositories returned HTTP 403 through the environment proxy. A real encode was therefore not claimed locally.
The GitHub Actions `video-pilot` mode installs FFmpeg and Noto CJK fonts, runs the real encoder/ffprobe checks,
and uploads `artifacts/`, `logs/` and the preview even when the job fails.
